    bibtex_key: orlitsky2016optimal
    category: theory-foundation
    role: foundation
    relevance: 'Provides the classical unseen-species framework for predicting future
      unseen mass from occupancy counts. EIBO uses it as the Good-Toulmin/missing-service-mass
      foundation for deployment-site open-set uncertainty.


      The DOI-associated PNAS record was resolved through the web search/fetch workflow;
      the source is used for the unseen-species method, not as evidence for QUIC-specific
      sampling.'
    abstract: ''
    semantic_scholar_id: ''
    verified: true
    added_by: ''
